	notes:
		!design Chumbeque
		If an effect would cause an opponent to discard a card while they have no cards in hand, they lose 3 life instead.
		!rul If a player has no cards in hand, you won’t be able to choose a card for effects like Duress, so the player won’t attempt to discard a card and lose life.
		Multiple Epic Fails will normally have no additional effect as there will be no more excess discards after the first has applied. It is possible they can apply if another replacement effect modifies the number of cards discarded after the first Epic Fail has taken effect.
		If an effect makes the discard optional in some way, such as "You may discard a card," "Discard up to two cards," or "Discard a card:," the opponent can’t attempt discard cards they don’t have to lose life.
		If an effect says a player "can’t discard cards," they will still lose life to Epic Fail if an effect would try to make them discard more cards than they have in hand.
		If a discard effect has a condition, Epic Fail will apply if they have fewer cards in hand than are attempting to be discarded, but not if they have enough cards in hand, just not enough that meet the condition.
		***Example*** Plague Calamity says "Target player reveals their hand and discards a nonland card." An opponent with no cards in hand will lose 3 life, a player with a single card in hand that is a land will not discard a card or lose 3 life, a player with a single card in hand that isn’t a land will discard that card.
		
